{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"Description updated during epic e369's plan review: the `RichTextCodec` this story formalizes is **also** the dependency J2 [rebar:62d9-9f6d-ecf4-4743] injects into the relocated `_sanitize_description` — that sanitizer's `fit_text_to_adf_limit` call IS this seam. J2 cannot move `jira_fields.py` wholesale (it imports the location-pinned `adf.py`), so the coupled sanitizers become contract-parameterized instead.\n\nEither landing order works: if J2 lands first with a minimal `Callable[[str], str]` fit placeholder, this story widens it to the full `RichTextCodec` and re-points the sanitizer. **What must never happen is `jira_family/` importing the pinned `adapters/jira/adf.py` directly.**\n\nBlocked by J2, so `review-plan` will fast-fail `INDETERMINATE` until J2 closes."},"env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1785338316538107001,"uuid":"9bef45a6-448d-411d-b788-6ffd2e1256b5"}